    "findings": {
        "DETERMINED PRECISION at the standing tolerance": "The worst-moving quantity of the T-1f pipeline is heightAtTargetForce at 1.195e-07 relative, so the SCF-derived part of the tree is determined to 6 significant digits and is printed to 9.",
        "COST of the honest direction": "Tightening the height tolerance from 1e-06 to 1e-09 costs 1.02x the SCF solves (288 against 282) at one design point.",
        "REACHABILITY of the honest direction": "The residual the height bracket works on is DISCONTINUOUS at every node-count boundary, M = round(h/dz). The largest jump measured is 9.787e-04 relative in the pressure over a logarithmic slope of -9.89, i.e. the root is indeterminate over 9.893e-05 in h - 4 determined digits - WHATEVER tolerance is asked for.",
        "BRACKET SEED - the movement P-15 produced": "The same residual and the same tolerance, reached from four different starting brackets, spread by 5.642e-07 relative in the solved height - 6 determined digits, against nine printed. This is the quantity CH-0043 is about, and it is the largest of the four probes.",
        "PATH NOISE": "Changing only the solve HISTORY - the warm field and the cache, same tolerance, same grid, same chain - moves stiffnessAtNineTenths by 9.180e-12 relative, i.e. 9 determined digits. The SCF field converges to 1e-11 in w, so the warm start is NOT what limits determinacy.",
        "THE CENSUS": "Six independent rounding implementations, not one: structure/ResultRounding.kt prints 9, determined 9; brush/FluctuationCorrectionStudy.kt prints 9, determined 6; brush/ScfDensityProfileStudy.kt prints 9, determined 6; window/WindowResultRounding.kt prints 9, determined 6; actuator/ActuatorResultRounding.kt prints 9, determined 4; coupling/CouplingResultRounding.kt prints 9, determined 5. Two carry different absolute floors (1e-9 and 1e-12).",
        "LADDER CHECK": "63 movements recorded over 6 tolerance rungs and one path-noise probe."
    },
    "validity": [
        "TRL 1-3. Nothing here is measured against an experiment. This is a statement about THIS repository's solvers, checked against their own DECLARED tolerances.",
        "ONE design point (10 nm, sigma = 0.0240 nm^-2, des Cloizeaux, dz = 0.2 nm). The determined precision is a property of a quantity and of a state; a sparser or more compressed layer may be pinned differently. The claim quotes the measured digits as an upper bound on what may be printed, not as the precision of every state.",
        "The tightest rung of the ladder is the reference, so every movement is a movement TOWARDS it and none is an error bar on it. The path-noise and grid-count probes are what bound the reference itself.",
        "No fluctuation, no grid convergence and no physics is re-derived here. The DISCRETISATION error of the SCF layer is far larger than any tolerance discussed - CLAUDE.md records the 10 nm stroke edge moving 23.4 % between dz = 0.4 and 0.2 nm - and that is a separate quantity from the determinacy of the emitted digits."
